            <ArticleTitle>Stent implantation without predilation in patients with a single, noncalcified coronary artery lesion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1250-3, A8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The purpose of this study was to assess the feasibility of stent implantation without predilation in patients with a single, noncalcified coronary artery lesion. A total of 122 patients were randomized to receive a stent with or without predilation; direct stent placement was possible in 59 of the 61 patients (97%) with an immediate and long-term clinical follow-up similar to that observed in the group of patients treated conventionally.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
